    "title": "Budget-three antipodal quotient pencil is primitive",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "The Mobius-welded antipodal map has exact odd degree d/4-1, so it cannot factor through a nontrivial cyclic or dihedral quotient of the dyadic subgroup. The direct index-four coset partition is also impossible: one deletion per coset gives four geometric-series factors with Vandermonde rank four, contradicting the rank-two pencil. The remaining quartic norm residual is primitive and nonperiodic.",
